  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Levetiracetam is an antiepileptic medicine used to treat epilepsy and various types of seizures, including focal, temporal lobe, frontal lobe, and tonic–clonic seizures. It is an approved drug widely used, with several products authorised in the European Union for epilepsy.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q417227&quot;>Wikidata Q417227</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>levetiracetam</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>N03AX14</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01202&quot;>DB01202</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/5284583&quot;>5284583</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:6437&quot;>6437</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q417227&quot;>Q417227</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C8H14N2O2</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>170.212 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
